From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:52:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: bound the unsafe string calls in the core engine

strcpy, strcat, sprintf and unterminated _snprintf/_vsnprintf calls in
src/universal, src/qcommon, src/script and src/stringed write without
knowing how large the destination is. Part 1 of 4 for upstream issue 8.

The replacements are the engine's own bounded forms (I_strncpyz,
I_strncat, Com_sprintf, Com_sprintfPos) and C99 snprintf/vsnprintf,
each given the destination's size. No MSVC *_s functions, so the code
stays portable.

This also fixes an off-by-one overflow in Info_SetValueForKey_Big and
bounds the assert report. va(), Com_sprintf and Com_sprintfPos keep
_vsnprintf, because their callers rely on -1 when the text is cut.
